From cc0c50abc6258b06d866dd90bfba2228bd828524 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valery Petrov <valerypetrov@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 23:26:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Leave a replica that may not answer the shard-target check to
 the check its own insert makes

The check asks each remote replica with SHOW CREATE TABLE and DESC TABLE,
which need SHOW COLUMNS on the table itself. A remote write needs less: the
shard's INSERT is authorized column by column, and a column-level grant
carries SHOW COLUMNS only on the columns it names, never on the table. A
cluster user holding exactly what the write sends could therefore perform
the write while being denied the check, whose refusal was counted as an
unverified replica and failed the request with ALL_CONNECTION_TRIES_FAILED.

Such a replica is now skipped instead. It is not left unchecked: the write
pins insert_expected_table_engine and insert_expected_column_types, so the
shard's own insert refuses the target it resolves unless it is still the
TimeSeries table of the type the wrapper declares. Every other failure to
answer is unchanged, and a read never refused an unverified replica anyway.

The test grants a cluster user only INSERT on the three columns a remote
write sends, of the shard-local table and of its inner tables, and proves
both statements the check makes are denied it while the write is
acknowledged; over the same credentials a same-schema MergeTree target is
still refused, now by the shard's own insert, which names the engine it
found and the one the INSERT expects.

